      "textEn": "49\n\nWhose can it be? Meaning: Although the demon was dead, his body had not lost its heat. This\nis extremely peculiar, because when a human or animal dies, their body immediately turns yellow\nand gradually becomes lighter and starts to rot. But here, although\nHiranyaksha had died, but the radiance of his body had not diminished because God had touched his\nbody. The body's vigor remains only as long as the soul is present.\nRemains. Although the soul had departed from the body of the demon, but by the touch of the body by God,\nits radiance did not diminish. The individual soul is different from the complete Supreme God.\nIf\nsomeone sees the complete Supreme Lord while leaving their body, then surely he\nis fortunate, therefore Brahma and other gods praised the death of that demon.\n\nThose yogis who are in yogic Samadhi,\nMeditate on the one who is in the state of being attached to the Linga, the seeker of liberation.\nThat demon king was struck by his feet,\nHe looked at his own body and was about to rise. 28 ”. Meaning of the word\n\nYam- that which; Yoginah- the yogi; Yoga- in the state of meditation; Rahah- in solitude; Dhyayanti- meditating;\nLi- from the body; Asat- false; Mumukshaya- with the desire for liberation; Tasya- his; Eshah- this; Daitya- of the demon; Diti's\nson; Rishabha:- the best jewel; Pada- from the feet; Aahata- struck down; Mukham- face; Prapashyanti- looking or gazing;\nTanum- the body; Utsarsar- released; Ha- without doubt..\n\nBrahma further said - Yogis, to be freed from their false physical bodies in Yogasamadhi,\nwhom they meditate on in solitude, this has been struck by the lotus feet of that Shri Bhagavan.\nIt has happened.\nAmong the sons of Diti, the crest jewel, seeing the face of God, has sacrificed his mortal\nbody. Meaning: This verse from the Shrimad Bhagavatam describes a yogic method. It is said\nthat the ultimate goal of yogis who meditate is to get rid of this physical body. Therefore, they meditate