      "textEn": "60\nChapter twenty\nMaitreya-Vidura conversation\nShaunaka said\nIn the middle of the establishment, Manu himself was born.\nKanyanvatishthadvaraani margayaavarajanam. 9>. Meaning of the word\n\nShaunakah-- Shaunakah; Uvachah-- said; Mahim-- to the earth; Pratishtham- situated; Adhyasya- having obtained; Saute-- O Suta\nGoswami; Swayambhuva- Swayambhuva; Manuh- by Manu; Kaani- what; Anvatishthat- having done; Dwarani- path; Margaya- for going;\nAvar- later; Janmanam- of those who are born..\n\nShri Shaunak asked--Hey Sut Goswami, when the earth was re-established in its orbit,\nwhat did Swayambhuva Manu do later to show the path of liberation to the people who were to be born? Meaning: The original pig incarnation of God happened during the time of Swayambhuva Manu, while the present\nera is the time of Vaivasvata Manu.\nThe duration of each Manu lasts for 72 times the cycle of the four Yugas,\nand each cycle is equivalent to 42,20,000 solar years. Therefore, the reign of one Manu\nlasts for 43,20,000 x 72 solar years. In each Manu's time, many types of changes occur,\nand in one day of Brahma, there are fourteen Manus. Here it is explained that for the salvation of those\ninhabited beings, Manu makes religious rules, who have come into this world for material enjoyment. God is so merciful that whoever comes into this world and wants to enjoy material pleasures,\nall the facilities of enjoyment are given to him, but along with that, the path to salvation\nis also open for him. Therefore, Shaunak Rishi asked Sut Goswami, ^“What did Swayambhuva Manu do after being re-established in his\nKakshya of the earth?”'\"\nKshatta Mahabhagavatah Krishnasya Ekantikah Suhrut.\nYastatyajagrajam Krishne Sapatyam Aghavaniti. 2). Lexicon"
