      "textEn": "66\n\nSut Goswami further said - Bharat's descendant Vidur, after listening to the story of God, was greatly\ndelighted because God, with his divine power, assuming the form of a pig,\nhad brought the earth up from the depths of the ocean in play (Leela), and Hiranyaksha\nwas killed with indifference. Then Vidura spoke to Maitreyi in this way. Meaning: here it is said that the god took the form of a pig with his power. Their form is not actually the form of a bound soul. A bound soul has to take a special body by the order of the supreme controller of the physical laws, but here it is clearly stated that\nGod did not have to take the form of a pig by being bound by any external power. In the Bhagavad Gita, this fact is also confirmed--when God descends to Earth, He assumes a form through His inner\npower. As a result, the form of God is never created from physical power.\nThis statement of the Mayavadis that whenever Brahma assumes any form,\nhe accepts it from Maya, is not valid because although Maya is superior to the bound soul,\nit is not superior to Shri Bhagavan, it is under His control, as it is confirmed in the Bhagavad Gita. Maya is under his supervision, Maya cannot transgress God. This\nMayaist ideology that the soul is the ultimate truth, but hidden by Maya, is invalid.\nBecause Maya is not so vast that it can hide God.\nThe power to conceal can be applied to a part of Brahma, but not to the Supreme Brahman.\n\nVidur said,\nThe lord of the universe, the creator, the progenitor, the lord of the universe,\nKimabhrutam me Brahmanprabhruhamvyaktam margavit. 9>. Meaning of the word\n\nVidur said-- Vidur said; Prajapati-patih-- Lord Brahma; Srutta-- by creating; Praja-sarge- to the creation of living beings; with the intention of creating; Prajapatin-- to the Prajapatis; Kim-- what; Arambhata-- began; Me- to the Muni; Brahman- Hey\nPious sage; Prabhuhi-- tell us; Avyakta-marg-vit-- the knower of those who do not know;\n\nVidur said- O holy sage, you also (explain) the subjects that are not understood by us"
